Proposed firmware change for round b150: print the previous boot's *kernel log*.

What it adds, and why it is a separate patch from 2026-11-12-panic-header-offsets.patch:

  * Include/UkePramLog.h (new, also under firmware/files/) is the single owner of the pram window's
    geometry and of the log record's format. Until now the window base/size were a #define inside
    UkeBootMemoryDxe.c; the kernel writer is documented against the same numbers, and this port's
    recurring failure mode is one fact in two places with only one updated. The header also carries the
    STATIC_ASSERTs that make a layout change fail the build instead of reading the wrong bytes.
  * UkeBootMemoryDxe.c gains ReadKernelLogRecord(), called once from the driver entry before the kernel
    that will overwrite the window is started. It prints the previous boot's kernel log as UKELOG: lines
    through DEBUG(), which is what lands in the Advanced Logger buffer that AdvancedLogDxe exports as
    log/<model>-<date>.log - the file a human already collects. Nothing is written: the reader is
    read-only, it validates the record (magic, version, commit word, length within the slot) before
    printing anything, and it prints one diagnostic line when there is no record, so "the kernel never
    wrote" cannot be mistaken for "the reader did not run".
  * It does not touch the panic path: the panic header stays at +0 and is parsed exactly as before (the
    same UKE_PANIC_HEADER_PREFIX at 0x14/0x18); the log record lives at +0x1C0000 with its own magic.

Apply it on a tree that already has 2026-11-12-panic-header-offsets.patch (b147), which is the state
round b147/b148 were built from:

    cd workspace/uefi-uke
    git apply ../uke-main-merge/firmware/2026-11-12-uke-log-record.patch
    cp -r ../uke-main-merge/firmware/files/Platforms .   # UkePramLog.h is untracked
    ./.venv-edk2/bin/python3 build_uefi.py -d uke -r DEBUG     # ~7 s

What that produces, verified here: Build/ukePkg/DEBUG_CLANGPDB/FV/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd
sha256 c7dcfca4e9686c4ac2ca01123a9b28a3df8cb3b3b2ad71a9d9f60868accebd45, and
Build/ukePkg/DEBUG_CLANGPDB/FV/Ffs/7E3A5B2C-...UkeBootMemoryDxe/*.ffs contains the string UKELOG.
work/round.py repacks that FD into work/flash/boot-round-b150-logpram.img (75a0948a...), whose gzip
payload contains the FD byte for byte.

Note for a reviewer: the same tree also carries unrelated uncommitted work (UkeUsbLogDxe, the handoff
and progress drivers). This patch is the diff of the two files above against that tree, not against
upstream, so it applies on top of it and touches nothing else.

